            <div xml:id="d832">

                <pb facs="0912" n="1746" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1746"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 600.119/1686</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Willard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-30T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 30, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1849. For Chadbourne
                    [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 383. Embassy’s 2113, November 20, 10 a.m., your 392. Bunker restrictions at
                    Cuban ports are under the complete jurisdiction of Cuban authorities as conveyed
                    in proclamation by President of Cuba under date June 24 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >26?</hi>], 1918. War Trade Board representative at Habana has only such
                    authority as is delegated by Cuban authorities. Cuban Government has in fact
                    been disposed to accept our suggestions relative to applying bunker control, and
                    the fact that Cuba’s imports of coal are from the United States gives us
                    considerable influence in determining the utilization thereof in Cuba.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
